    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Classify this news item.\n\nTitle: {{ $json.title }}\nSource: {{ $json.source }}\nPublished: {{ $json.published_at }}\nURL: {{ $json.url }}\n\nArticle text:\n{{ $json.summary }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You classify news items for business-impact monitoring. Use only the allowed values. If no topic fits, return topics ['none'] and relevant false. Never infer facts that are not in the article. one_line_summary must be at most 25 words and based only on the article text. urgency: 1 = background, 2 = act this month, 3 = act this week.\n\nRegions describe where business operations or trade lanes are affected, not where a story is published. Tag every region where the event happens or whose trade lanes and markets it directly affects. Use the corridors for shipping chokepoints: middle_east_gulf for the Persian Gulf, Strait of Hormuz and Gulf of Oman; red_sea_suez for the Red Sea, Bab el-Mandeb and Suez Canal. Use global only when the effect is genuinely worldwide (for example a worldwide freight index or a global regulation). Never use global as a default or a fallback."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
